{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Instance Segmentation \u2014 Mask R-CNN Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: RoIAlign from scratch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "This is the one component of Mask R-CNN that is simpler to understand as code than as prose."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn.functional as F"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def roi_align_single(feature, box, output_size=7, spatial_scale=1 / 16.0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    feature: (C, H, W) single-image feature map"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    box: (x1, y1, x2, y2) in original image pixel coordinates"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    output_size: side of the output grid (7 for box head, 14 for mask head)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    spatial_scale: reciprocal of the feature map stride"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    C, H, W = feature.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x1, y1, x2, y2 = [c * spatial_scale - 0.5 for c in box]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    bin_w = (x2 - x1) / output_size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    bin_h = (y2 - y1) / output_size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    grid_y = torch.linspace(y1 + bin_h / 2, y2 - bin_h / 2, output_size)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    grid_x = torch.linspace(x1 + bin_w / 2, x2 - bin_w / 2, output_size)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    yy, xx = torch.meshgrid(grid_y, grid_x, indexing=\"ij\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    gx = 2 * (xx + 0.5) / W - 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    gy = 2 * (yy + 0.5) / H - 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    grid = torch.stack([gx, gy], dim=-1).unsqueeze(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sampled = F.grid_sample(feature.unsqueeze(0), grid, mode=\"bilinear\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                            align_corners=False)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return sampled.squeeze(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Every number is at a bilinearly-sampled position. No rounding, no quantisation, no dropped gradients."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Compare to torchvision's RoIAlign"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from torchvision.ops import roi_align"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "feature = torch.randn(1, 16, 50, 50)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "boxes = torch.tensor([[0, 10, 20, 100, 90]], dtype=torch.float32)  # (batch_idx, x1, y1, x2, y2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "ours = roi_align_single(feature[0], boxes[0, 1:].tolist(), output_size=7, spatial_scale=1/4)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "theirs = roi_align(feature, boxes, output_size=(7, 7), spatial_scale=1/4, sampling_ratio=1, aligned=True)[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"shape ours:   {tuple(ours.shape)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"shape theirs: {tuple(theirs.shape)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"max|diff|:    {(ours - theirs).abs().max().item():.3e}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "With `sampling_ratio=1` and `aligned=True`, the two match to within `1e-5`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Load a pretrained Mask R-CNN"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from torchvision.models.detection import maskrcnn_resnet50_fpn_v2, MaskRCNN_ResNet50_FPN_V2_Weights"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model = maskrcnn_resnet50_fpn_v2(weights=MaskRCNN_ResNet50_FPN_V2_Weights.DEFAULT)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model.eval()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"params: {sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters()):,}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"classes (including background): {len(model.roi_heads.box_predictor.cls_score.out_features * [0])}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "46M parameters, 91 classes (COCO). The first class (id 0) is background; everything the model actually detects starts at id 1."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Run inference"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "with torch.no_grad():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = torch.randn(3, 400, 600)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    predictions = model([x])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "p = predictions[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"boxes:  {tuple(p['boxes'].shape)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"labels: {tuple(p['labels'].shape)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"scores: {tuple(p['scores'].shape)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"masks:  {tuple(p['masks'].shape)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The mask tensor is shape `(N, 1, H, W)`. Threshold at 0.5 to get a binary mask per object:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "binary_masks = (p['masks'] > 0.5).squeeze(1)  # (N, H, W) boolean"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Swap the heads for a custom class count"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The common fine-tuning recipe: reuse the backbone, FPN, and RPN; replace the two classifier heads."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from torchvision.models.detection.faster_rcnn import FastRCNNPredictor"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from torchvision.models.detection.mask_rcnn import MaskRCNNPredictor"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def build_custom_maskrcnn(num_classes):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model = maskrcnn_resnet50_fpn_v2(weights=MaskRCNN_ResNet50_FPN_V2_Weights.DEFAULT)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    in_features = model.roi_heads.box_predictor.cls_score.in_features"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model.roi_heads.box_predictor = FastRCNNPredictor(in_features, num_classes)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    in_features_mask = model.roi_heads.mask_predictor.conv5_mask.in_channels"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    hidden_layer = 256"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model.roi_heads.mask_predictor = MaskRCNNPredictor(in_features_mask, hidden_layer, num_classes)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return model"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "custom = build_custom_maskrcnn(num_classes=5)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"custom cls_score.out_features: {custom.roi_heads.box_predictor.cls_score.out_features}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`num_classes` must include the background class, so a dataset with 4 object classes uses `num_classes=5`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 6: Freeze what does not need training"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "On small datasets, freeze the backbone and the FPN. Only the RPN objectness + regression and the two heads learn."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def freeze_backbone_and_fpn(model):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    # torchvision Mask R-CNN packs the FPN inside `model.backbone` (as"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    # `model.backbone.fpn`), so iterating `model.backbone.parameters()` covers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    # both the ResNet feature layers and the FPN lateral/output convs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for p in model.backbone.parameters():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        p.requires_grad = False"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return model"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "custom = freeze_backbone_and_fpn(custom)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "trainable = sum(p.numel() for p in custom.parameters() if p.requires_grad)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"trainable after freeze: {trainable:,}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "On 500-image datasets this is the difference between convergence and overfitting."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **(Easy)** Verify your RoIAlign against `torchvision.ops.roi_align` on 100 random boxes. Report the max absolute difference. Also run RoIPool (pre-2017 behaviour) and show it diverges by ~1-2 feature-map pixels on boxes near the border.\n2. **(Medium)** Fine-tune `maskrcnn_resnet50_fpn_v2` on a 50-image custom dataset (any two classes: balloons, fish, pothole, logos). Freeze the backbone, train for 20 epochs, report mask AP@0.5.\n3. **(Hard)** Replace Mask R-CNN's mask head with one that predicts at 56x56 instead of 28x28. Measure mAP@IoU=0.75 before and after. Explain why the gain (or lack of one) matches the expected boundary-precision / memory trade-off."
      ]
    }
